  "worked_solution": "A partition of a set $X$ is a collection of non-empty subsets of $X$ where every element of $X$ is contained in *exactly* one subset. \n\nTo find the subset that goes in the blank, we must identify which elements of $X$ are not yet contained within any of the given subsets.\n\nLet's go through each element of $X$ and check:\n\n- $3$ does not belong to any of the given subsets $\\,\\times $\n\n- $6\\in {6,12,18}\\,\u2713$\n\n- $9$ does not belong to any of the given subsets $\\,\\times $\n\n- $12\\in {6,12,18}\\,\u2713$\n\n- $15\\in {15,21}\\,\u2713$\n\n- $18\\in {6,12,18}\\,\u2713$\n\n- $21\\in {15,21}\\,\u2713$\n\n- $24$ does not belong to any of the given subsets $\\,\\times $\n\nThe elements $3,$ $9,$ and $24$ are not yet contained within any of the given subsets. Therefore, the subset that must go in the blank is ${3,9,24}.$",
